#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:43
#: 26f0c7612c7d410798cfca64bc36de81
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:44
#: f62abbdb75a24627b4a06b7de3f0033f
msgid "RC input is configured by default via the USART3 RX input. It supports all serial RC protocols except PPM and SBUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:46
#: 805f0edd54c64fc380e5b7326498ff24
msgid "Note: If the receiver is FPort the receiver must be tied to the USART3 TX pin using an external bi-directional inverter, :ref:`RSSI_TYPE<RSSI_TYPE>` set to 3, and :ref:`SERIAL3_OPTIONS<SERIAL3_OPTIONS>` must be set to 7 (invert TX/RX, half duplex). For full duplex like CRSF/ELRS use both RX3 and TX3 and set RSSI_TYPE also to 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:49
#: f61ba84763314ae3ae23782070565ef4
msgid "The SBUS pad uses a hardware inverter connected to USART2_RX. If you wish to use SBUS then set :ref:`SERIAL3_PROTOCOL<SERIAL3_PROTOCOL>` to something other than \"23\" and set :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` to \"23\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:52
#: 131ce65ad05a4af28ce9172e94fa88d9
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:53
#: 6f9961254db543c7933589a9fd8580cf
msgid "Onboard OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver) is supported by default. Simultaneously, DisplayPort OSD is available on the HD VTX connector by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:56
#: e33a6b665a0444ce839ce2c0f341d34a
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:57
#: 3403eb81131c48bfbbe31013abc33eb6
msgid "The SPEDIX F405 supports up to 9 PWM outputs. The pads for motor output M1 to M8 are provided on both the motor connectors and on separate pads, plus M9 on a separate pad for LED strip (default configuration) or another PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:61
#: d1ac946c985343a5b0c11798afd44f47
msgid "The PWM is in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:63
#: ac6bf5a9a756463f818c9c684cd0f5df
msgid "PWM 1-4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:64
#: 990134006bf944759577f4b3978cafbf
msgid "PWM 5-6 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:65
#: 74116f43945a490aab2f228478176e8c
msgid "PWM 7-8 in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:66
#: 77f47fb36772457bb553536ebe252f65
msgid "PWM 9 in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:68
#: 0a9c041ee5f34ea0b74995febc64082c
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Channels 1-4 support bi-directional dshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:73
#: 3899dc5cf12b496bad8d9b17415dcf68
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:74
#: 2e4b11a8c0b64db0b5e0af0bc70f69c7
msgid "The board has a built-in voltage sensor and external current sensor input. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries. The correct battery setting parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:77
#: 059fb6656736412ba610ea53cda38eb4
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:78
#: a3dd6dca0d254a1bb1d4e234819a2268
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:79
#: aba99bae1ea84abaa0de05c1d4bd2e7d
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11 (CURR pin)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:80
#: aa581082c7784016b9b2410d4c21c665
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:81
#: 6bc7d8c2769b4e3aab6b8e4a3145a0df
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 50"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:84
#: cfd57d2ecb724095ae9c61e34b3c9223
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:85
#: f71aa43369b741d291888777ce72ebee
msgid "The board has no onboard compass. External compass modules can be connected via the I2C bus (SDA/SCL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:88
#: bace4381543746708c02576d50ea9582
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:89
#: dfd263415b9140458edc6d585deee8b8
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the camera output to the connectors marked \"CAM1\" and \"CAM2\". Setting this GPIO low switches the video output from CAM1 to CAM2. By default RELAY3 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-spedixf405.rst:92
